n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let us justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\n3x=O({{3x}_{⏟}}_{f}).\n$$\n\nThis is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\n3x=O(3x),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\n-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=O(2x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and $\\text{the sum property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O(5x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line  $\\text{L4}$   we have\n\n$$\nf=O(5x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0,\n$$\n\nand by the $\\text{constant multiple property}$ with $c=5,$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$" 13194139534816 true] [17592186311934 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311935 13194139534816 true] [17592186311934 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311936 13194139534816 true] [17592186311934 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311937 13194139534816 true] [17592186311934 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311938 13194139534816 true] [17592186311934 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311939 13194139534816 true] [17592186311934 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139534816 true] [17592186311934 1041 "field-1" 13194139534816 true] [17592186311934 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311939 13194139534816 true] [17592186311934 1110 #uuid "8e8733d0-4555-50d8-84be-1528ecde2ebf" 13194139534816 true] [17592186311935 1034 "the absorption property" 13194139534816 true] [17592186311935 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534816 true] [17592186311935 1111 #uuid "debf6873-0622-578b-b420-859033d3d8c8" 13194139534816 true] [17592186311936 1034 "the constant multiple property" 13194139534816 true] [17592186311936 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534816 true] [17592186311936 1111 #uuid "11c54f67-458b-5dab-af5f-930a2e7